{#
    Example template override — safe to delete if you don't need it.

    This follows the pattern from the "Creating Themes" guide:
    https://docs.forumify.net/guides/theme#templates

    It extends the ORIGINAL core template (via the `@!` prefix) and only
    wraps its output, so it keeps working even if forumify updates the
    forum list template internally.

    Template overrides only work for blocks the core template actually
    defines. At the time of writing, block coverage varies by template —
    inspect the installed version's .html.twig files (or ask in the
    forumify Discord) to confirm which blocks are available for the
    page you want to customize, then copy this pattern for it.
#}
{% extends '@!Forumify/frontend/forum/list.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="flex-1">
            {{ parent() }}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
